Brute Force Approach:
class Solution {
    public void sort012(int[] arr) {
        // code here
        int count0=0,count1=0,count2=0;
        for(int i=0;i<arr.length;i++){
            if(arr[i]==0) count0++;
            else if(arr[i]==1) count1++;
            else count2++;
        }
        int i=0;
        while(count0 >0){
            arr[i]=0;
            i++;
            count0--;
        }
        while(count1 > 0){
            arr[i]=1;
            i++;
            count1--;
        }
        while(count2 > 0){
            arr[i]=2;
            i++;
            count2--;
        }
    }
}



Optimize Approach:
🌈 Dutch National Flag Algorithm
[2, 0, 2, 1, 1, 0]

        ↓
[0, 0, 1, 1, 2, 2]
The three pointers
int left = 0;
int mid = 0;
int high = nums.length - 1;

Think of the array as divided into four regions:
0s        1s          Unknown        2s
↓         ↓              ↓             ↓
[  0  0  |  1  1  |  ?  ?  ?  |  2  2  ]
          ↑             ↑             ↑
        left           mid           high

More precisely:
[0 ... left-1]     = all 0
[left ... mid-1]   = all 1
[mid ... high]     = UNKNOWN
[high+1 ... n-1]   = all 2


class Solution {
    public void sortColors(int[] nums) {
        int left=0;
        int mid=0;
        int high=nums.length-1;
        while(mid<= high){
            if(nums[mid]==0){
                int temp=nums[left];
                nums[left]=nums[mid];
                nums[mid]=temp;
                left++;
                mid++;

            }else if(nums[mid]==1){
                mid++;

            }else{
                int temp=nums[high];
                nums[high]=nums[mid];
                nums[mid]=temp;
                high--;

            }
        }
        
    }
}

Time = O(n)
Space = O(1)
